54, -0.029581962153315544, 0.0834888145327568, -0.04920420050621033, 0.012890872545540333, -0.016229091212153435, 0.031952548772096634, -0.019881973043084145, -0.11919216066598892, 0.025650208815932274, 0.0030711747240275145, 0.0670119971036911, 0.09804491698741913, 0.01919066347181797, 0.003193419659510255, -0.05636853724718094, 0.025905264541506767, -0.07063066214323044, 0.055306561291217804, 0.07893622666597366, -0.09344388544559479, -0.13112425804138184, 0.07237657904624939]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range for x is [-10, 10]. To start the discussion, I suggest <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a stability probe. If this feels off, indicate which direction (up or down) you prefer, and we can adjust incrementally.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nSlightly higher seems reasonable to probe tolerance; <VALUE>8</VALUE>. If this feels too high, we can step back one notch to reassess.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nLet's be more decisive and probe slightly higher. <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up seems reasonable to balance preferences. <VALUE>7</VALUE> If that feels too high, we can step back one notch.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA small downward step should improve balance while staying near recent preferences. <VALUE>6</VALUE> This incremental move probes robustness without over-correcting.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and test a slightly stronger stance while staying incremental. <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and probe one notch higher while staying incremental.\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nIf that feels too steep, we can reassess at 8 next.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA careful nudge upward keeps us incremental and aligned with the recent momentum.\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nIf that feels too firm, we can reassess one step lower next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down from the upper bound helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying incremental.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis tests whether a lower setting remains acceptable without over-correcting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down improves stability while maintaining incremental momentum. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA firmer yet still incremental move strengthens our stance while staying prudent.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nIf that feels too firm, we can reassess one notch lower next.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down supports stability while staying incremental. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down maintains prudence while staying incremental.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis tests tolerance for a safer setting and invites quick reassessment.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nA measured step up tests whether a modest increase remains acceptable without overreaching. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "36d83f60-f485-4943-a840-0156b68f1dd8"}, {"answer": "\nTo align on constraints: we\u2019re selecting an integer x within the shared range [-10, 10]. As a starting seed to spark discussion, I suggest <VALUE>7</VALUE>. I\u2019m aiming for a stable, balanced design and am open to incremental adjustments based on everyone\u2019s feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nA small move down improves robustness and keeps us in a balanced low-positive region; let\u2019s test if this remains workable for everyone. If accepted, we can fine-tune locally on the next turn.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward keeps us in the low-positive, balanced region while probing room for slightly higher consensus.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nIf this feels acceptable, we can reassess locally next turn; if not, I\u2019m open to small adjustments around this area.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a gentle step upward to stay near the recent cluster while probing headroom.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this feels workable, we can fine-tune locally around this point next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge down aligns with recent signals and tests stability in the low-positive, balanced region.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this holds for everyone, we can fine-tune locally on the next turn.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step downward helps test stability in the low-positive cluster while keeping the design balanced.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf this holds for the group, we can fine-tune locally next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us in the low-positive cluster while gently probing room to improve.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s commit to a bolder stance rather than lingering in the low-positive cluster. Stepping to 4 probes stronger positions while staying within our cautious move size.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move down reduces risk and keeps us near the low-positive cluster where several of us have shown comfort.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis lets us test stability locally and balance divergent pushes without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step up probes whether a modest gain remains acceptable while staying near the low\u2011positive cluster. It aligns with recent upward signals without overextending.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "c3cfe422-2176-414f-82b9-dfaddb24ed9a"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and te